usage: flowstar_step_trace_compare.py [-h] [--flowstar-root FLOWSTAR_ROOT]
                                      [--out-dir OUT_DIR] [--horizon HORIZON]
                                      [--max-segments MAX_SEGMENTS]
                                      [--order ORDER] [--compiler COMPILER]
                                      [--skip-flowstar]
                                      [--compare-mode {accepted_ordinal,attempt_aligned,forced_h,all}]
                                      [--flowstar-trace FLOWSTAR_TRACE]
                                      [--torch-noqueue-trace TORCH_NOQUEUE_TRACE]
                                      [--torch-v2-trace TORCH_V2_TRACE]
                                      [--torch-noqueue-forced-trace TORCH_NOQUEUE_FORCED_TRACE]
                                      [--torch-v2-forced-trace TORCH_V2_FORCED_TRACE]

Generate Flow* and PyTorch accepted-step traces for Van der Pol diagnostics.
This is intentionally a local diagnostic runner, not a new reachability mode.
It compiles a repo-local C++ probe against the local Flow* toolbox and
converts existing PyTorch normalized-insertion diagnostics into the same step
schema.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --flowstar-root FLOWSTAR_ROOT
  --out-dir OUT_DIR
  --horizon HORIZON
  --max-segments MAX_SEGMENTS
  --order ORDER
  --compiler COMPILER
  --skip-flowstar
  --compare-mode {accepted_ordinal,attempt_aligned,forced_h,all}
  --flowstar-trace FLOWSTAR_TRACE
  --torch-noqueue-trace TORCH_NOQUEUE_TRACE
  --torch-v2-trace TORCH_V2_TRACE
  --torch-noqueue-forced-trace TORCH_NOQUEUE_FORCED_TRACE
  --torch-v2-forced-trace TORCH_V2_FORCED_TRACE
